cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BALINA in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "BALINA: Bayesian And Logical Influence-diagram Network Application"
abstract: "An interactive tool for building, analysing and learning Bayesian networks and influence diagrams. BALINA combines a graphical editor with exact probabilistic inference (junction tree), decision analysis (maximum expected utility and optimal policies), parameter learning (Dirichlet priors, EM), structure learning (PC, Hill-Climbing, Tabu Search, MMHC), sensitivity analysis and stochastic simulation. It reads and writes XMLBIF and GeNIe/SMILE files and CSV case data, and runs natively (Rust) and in the browser (WebAssembly)."
